## 2. Hard rules

1. **Presentation only.** You may change JSX markup structure, classNames, styles, and
   add purely presentational components.
2. **Do NOT change:** hook logic (`useState/useEffect/useMemo/useCallback`), data
   fetching, API URLs and params, data mapping/normalising, event-handler logic, props
   passed between components, navigation targets and query params, filter/sort/
   pagination logic, Excel export, phone masking, `ptpEngine`/`interactions` helpers,
   or any label/copy text.
3. **Nothing disappears.** Every data field currently shown must still be shown. Every
   button, link, filter, tab, export and drawer must still exist and behave the same.
   You may regroup, restyle, collapse into an expander, or reorder, but not remove.
4. **Render-time formatting is allowed** (₹ with Indian grouping, consistent date
   display). Never mutate the underlying data. Exports must still use raw values.
5. **Bugs: report, don't fix.** If you find a logic/routing/security bug, add it to
   `CII_REDESIGN_NOTES.md` (file, line, description) and leave the code alone.
6. **Isolation.** Every CII page root is wrapped in `<div className="cii-app">`.
   All new CSS lives in `src/cii/cii.css` (imported only by CII files). Do not edit
   global CSS and never rely on the root `text-align:center`.
7. After each task run `npm run lint` and `npm run build`, and show
   `git diff --name-only`. Any changed file outside section 1's allowed list gets
   reverted.
8. If this spec mentions a field that does not exist in the code, ignore it. If the
   code has fields this spec doesn't mention, KEEP them and place them in the most
   logical group.

