| channel: WhatsApp | `#067647` | |

**Priority and score scale (use everywhere, identically):**
P1 / lowest score band = danger. P2 / middle band = warning. P3 / highest band = success
(or info for neutral states). Use the thresholds the code ALREADY uses. Do not invent
new thresholds. Wherever a score or priority appears in a list, show a tiny legend or a
tooltip explaining the colors.

### 3.3 Typography
- Font stack: `Inter, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif`.
- Sizes: 12 (labels, captions, chips), 13 (table body), 14 (body), 16 (card titles),
  20 (page title), 24 (large KPI numbers). Weights 400, 500, 600 only.
- Numbers, money, DPD and counts use `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`.
- Field labels: sentence case, 12px, `--cii-text-3`. Do NOT use long all-caps labels.
  All-caps is allowed only for tiny status chips (11px, letter-spacing .04em).
- Left-align all text. Right-align numeric table columns. Center only icons, avatars,
  empty states and gauge numbers.

### 3.4 Shape, spacing, elevation
- 4px spacing grid (4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32).
- Radius: 8px for inputs/buttons/chips-rects, 12px for cards, 999px for pills/avatars.
- Single shadow: `0 1px 2px rgba(16,24,40,.06)`. Drawers/modals: `0 12px 32px rgba(16,24,40,.18)`.
- **No** gradients, glassmorphism, blurred backgrounds, emoji, or coin/gold icons.
- Icons: `lucide-react`, 16px (20px in empty states), stroke 1.75, color `--cii-text-3`
  unless meaningful. Do not hand-draw SVG icon sets.

### 3.5 Layout and density
- Design for **1366×768** first; scale up to 1920 with a fluid max-width of 1440px.
- Sticky header 56px. Page padding 24px (16px under 1024px). Section gap 16px.
- Page title row: title 20px/600 + one-line muted description (max one line) + actions
  on the right. NO hero banners, NO big marketing paragraphs.
- Tables: header row sticky inside its scroll container, 44px body rows (single-line
  cells, ellipsis + `title` tooltip for overflow), 36px compact variant for very dense
  tables. Hover row `#F9FAFB`. Selected row `--cii-primary-tint`. Wide tables scroll
  horizontally inside their own container, never the page.
- Chips never wrap (`white-space: nowrap`).
- Cards: white, 1px border, 12px radius, 16px padding, optional title row with a
  16px/600 title and right-aligned actions.

### 3.6 Components to build in `src/cii/ui/` (presentational only)
`PageHeader`, `Card`, `KpiTile`, `Button` (primary / secondary / ghost / danger),
`StatusPill`, `ChannelBadge`, `PriorityChip`, `ScoreBar`, `ScoreRing` (replaces the
conic-gradient/SVG gauges), `KeyValueGrid`, `Tabs` (underline style, controlled),
`SegmentedControl`, `FilterBar`, `DataTable` styles, `Drawer` shell (styling only; keep
each page's existing open/close logic), `Modal` shell, `EmptyState`, `ErrorBanner`,
`Skeleton`, `CopyableId` (muted small mono text with a copy icon).
Plus `src/cii/format.js` with pure helpers: `inr(n)` → `₹16,36,029` (en-IN grouping),
`dateTime(d)` → `13 Oct 2026, 12:09 pm`, `dateOnly(d)` → `13 Oct 2026`, `compact(n)`.

### 3.7 States
- **Loading:** skeletons shaped like the final content (not spinners over blank pages).
- **Error:** inline `ErrorBanner` with the message and the page's EXISTING retry handler.
- **Empty:** `EmptyState` (icon, one line title, one line hint) ONLY when data is
  genuinely absent (`null`, `undefined`, empty list). Never render `0/100` gauges or rows
  of `—` as if they were real results when the underlying value is absent. If you can't
  tell absent from a real zero, leave the code's behavior and log it in the notes file.
- Raw IDs/UUIDs are never primary text. Show them muted via `CopyableId`.

### 3.8 Accessibility
Visible focus ring (2px `--cii-primary`, 2px offset). Clickable `<div>`s get
`role="button"`, `tabIndex={0}` and Enter/Space handlers that call the EXISTING onClick.
Icon-only buttons need `aria-label`. Text contrast at least 4.5:1. Every table cell
count matches its header (fix `colSpan` mismatches). Inputs have labels or aria-labels.
Status is never conveyed by color alone (always text or icon).

